# PROLOGUE — "Soundcheck", part 2: the alley behind the Pink Wyvern, and the first fight.
# Canon: the storyboard doc (v2). Rex is a Danny Zuko greaser: "Whoa, whoa, whoa", "dweeb", "doll", third person when impressed.
# Objectives come from src/content/objectives.ts; repeat examines branch on seen.<scene id>.

@scene prologue.the_letter
# PLOT: The Cyrano letters (Rex can't read), Rex's "only I bully Adder" code, and the dock crew's grudge that starts the first fight.
# CHARACTER: Rex's ego and buried decency; Eddar's talent, wit and quiet nerve when he climbs out of the bin to stand beside him.
@bgm alley_rex
@cam focus rex
NARRATOR: Fryer steam and sea salt. Rex Valor leans on the dumpster like it owes him rent, combing his pompadour. Grubb holds the mirror.
REX [smug]: Whoa, whoa, whoa. Adder. My man. My scribe. My little pencil.
EDDAR: Rex. In an alley, of your own free will. Has the boardwalk run out of mirrors?
REX: Rex goes where Rex is needed, dweeb. And tonight Rex needs a letter.
GRUBB: Rex needs a letter!
REX: Thanks, Grubb.
NARRATOR: The comb pauses.
REX [smug]: Princess Lyra. Solara. Sky city. Hair like a sunset on a Tuesday. When I win the Great Fracas, she's gonna have a letter from me in her hand.
REX: Which is soon. Any day now. So. Pencil out. "Dear Princess. You're hot."
EDDAR: A noble opening. Brief, like a lightning strike, and about as subtle.
? Write it beautifully. -> beautiful {harmony:+1}
? Write it beautifully, with one small joke at Rex's expense. -> joke {bond_rex:-1}
? Write exactly what he said. -> literal {bond_rex:-2}
* literal
EDDAR: "Dear Princess. You're hot." Signed, Rex. Shall I read it back?
REX: ...
REX [hurt]: Adder. Rex pays you three tokens a letter 'cause Rex is a GENEROUS LEGEND, not 'cause he wants to sound like Grubb.
GRUBB: Hey.
REX: Do it right, dweeb.
@goto beautiful
* joke
@flag p.joke
EDDAR: Writing. "...and though I am but a humble jouster, with hair no mortal comb has ever tamed..."
REX [smile]: Ha! That's good. That's true. Keep that.
* beautiful
EDDAR: "Princess. They say the sky above Solara never truly darkens, that your towers hold the last of every sunset like a held breath."
EDDAR: "I have never seen it. Yet I think I know the feeling, for there are people who enter a room, and the night forgets itself."
GRUBB: ...Whoa.
REX [hurt]: ...Yeah. Yeah, that's what Rex meant. Seal it, Adder. Rex's eyes are tired.
@sfx coins
@set tokens += 4
@set bond_rex += 1
NARRATOR: He pays four tokens. Then he lifts Eddar by the jacket, one-handed, and posts him into the trash barrel like a letter.
@sfx barrel
@cam shake
EDDAR: Ah. The traditional postage.
REX [smug]: Can't break tradition on festival night, Adder. Bad luck.
@flag p.vinnie_in
@cam focus vinnie
VINNIE: HA! Look at mop boy! In the BIN, where he LIVES!
NARRATOR: Rex turns. Slowly. He snaps the comb shut.
REX: Hey.
REX [angry]: Hey. Nobody pushes Adder around but me.
@sfx punch
@cam shake
NARRATOR: One punch. Vinnie is suddenly lying down, elsewhere, reconsidering his life.
REX [smug]: You're welcome, dweeb.
GRUBB: You're welcome, dweeb!
@flag p.letter_done
@flag p.crew_in
@cam focus vinnie
NARRATOR: Vinnie staggers up. Behind him, two more dockworkers fill the alley mouth: Brick, who is a wall, and Moss, who carries a hook for some reason.
VINNIE [angry]: Big man with a pauldron. Let's see you do that to three of us.
REX [smug]: Whoa, whoa, whoa. Three? On the Valor? That's not a fight, that's a fan club.
GRUBB: I'll... hold your drink, Rex!
@cmd exit_npc grubb back
@flag p.grubb_fled
NARRATOR: Grubb flees, holding no drink.
@sfx clunk
NARRATOR: The barrel lid clangs. Eddar climbs out, picks a dented trash-can lid off the cobbles, and holds it like a shield.
EDDAR: I'd counsel peace, gentlemen. But I see your minds are made, and the alley, alas, is narrow.
REX: Adder? Get back in the bin, I got this.
EDDAR: You've got two of them, Rex. I'll keep the third from your back. It's only arithmetic.
@battle dock_crew
@end

@scene prologue.after_dock_fight
# PLOT: The crew flees; Rex and Eddar head inside together, which carries Rex into the Champion scene.
# CHARACTER: Rex's backhanded respect; Eddar's grace and his ache, in the Ledger.
@bgm alley_rex
VINNIE [angry]: This ain't over, mop boy!
EDDAR: It rarely is, Vinnie. That's the tragedy of it.
@cmd exit_npc vinnie back
@cmd exit_npc brick back
@cmd exit_npc moss back
@flag p.crew_fled
@sfx coins
@set tokens += 6
REX [smile]: Not bad, Adder. You hit like a librarian, but you hit like a smart librarian.
EDDAR: High praise, from a man who's never met one.
REX [smug]: C'mon. Rex is thirsty, and Mama Dee's got a corner booth with my name on it. Probably. Rex should check.
LEDGER: Entry #2,207: Fought three men in an alley with a bin lid, beside the man who put me in the bin. Life is not a story; a story would be ashamed of such symmetry.
@warp wyvern from_alley
@end

@scene prologue.vinnie
# CHARACTER: a bully's bully, horizontal; Eddar is kind to him anyway. (Reachable only if the player walks over before the crew arrives.)
VINNIE: Ugh. Is the alley supposed to be spinning?
EDDAR: Only on festival night. Stay down, Vinnie. Something tells me your friends will be along to collect you.
@end

@scene prologue.dock_crew
# CHARACTER: two more mouths for Vinnie's grudge.
BRICK: ...
EDDAR: Brick says nothing. Brick doesn't need to. Brick is a sentence with no verbs.
@end

@scene prologue.dumpster
# CHARACTER: Eddar's dry dignity.
@if seen.prologue.dumpster>=1
EDDAR: Trash: out. Dignity: also out, but in a separate bag.
@end
@endif
@sfx trash
EDDAR: Rex leaned on this like it owed him rent. It does, in a sense. We all owe this dumpster something.
@end

@scene prologue.barrel
# CHARACTER: running gag; Eddar's grace under humiliation.
@if p.letter_done
@if seen.prologue.barrel>=2
EDDAR: Some men have a family crest. I have a barrel. Same thing, structurally.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: My barrel. We've been through a lot together. More than I've been through with most people.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: A trash barrel. Clean, as trash barrels go. Rex has standards.
@end

@scene prologue.cat
# CHARACTER: Eddar's gentleness. Encore will matter later (she always comes back).
@if seen.prologue.cat>=1
EDDAR: Encore blinks at me, slowly. In cat, that's either "I love you" or "you are furniture." I'll take either.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: The alley cat. Mama Dee calls her Encore, because she always comes back.
EDDAR: She judges me less than everyone inside. I bring her fish.
@end

@scene prologue.exit_sign
# CHARACTER: the quiet ache under the jokes.
@if seen.prologue.exit_sign>=1
EDDAR: It flickers on the X. EIT. Even the way out isn't sure of itself tonight.
@end
@endif
EDDAR: A neon EXIT sign, buzzing pink. Every night it tells me there's a way out. Every night I go back inside.
@end

@scene prologue.alley_mouth
# PLOT: Soft wall. Before the Bellshell: festival crowds. After: the Main Drag, which is the next storyboard.
@if p.bellshell_done
EDDAR: The Main Drag, and screaming all down it. Every way out of here leads into that. (The Main Drag opens in the next build.)
@end
@endif
EDDAR: Out there it's all paper meteors and people practising their applause. Mama Dee would find me. She always finds me.
@end
